{
  "info": {
    "name": "SupportIQ — AI Customer Support Intelligence",
    "_postman_id": "supportiq-demo-v1",
    "description": "Complete SupportIQ demo collection.\n\nCovers the full AI-powered support flow:\n  → Ticket CRUD\n  → Raw email analysis (HERO endpoint)\n  → Per-ticket AI analysis + auto-escalation\n  → AI-drafted professional replies\n  → Live AI dashboard\n  → Bulk triage / urgency ranking\n  → Escalation queue\n\nSet the `baseUrl` variable before running (default: http://localhost:8080).\nTicket IDs 1–20 are pre-seeded by SupportDataInitializer on startup.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "ticketId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Set automatically by '01 Create Ticket' test script, or set manually to any seeded ticket ID (1-20)"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 — Ticket Management (CRUD)",
      "description": "Basic ticket lifecycle — create, read, update, delete.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 Create Ticket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has ticketNumber', () => pm.expect(j.ticketNumber).to.match(/TKT-\\d{4}/));",
                  "pm.test('Status is OPEN', () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('OPEN'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('ticketId', j.id);",
                  "console.log('Created ticket id=' + j.id + ' number=' + j.ticketNumber);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"customerName\": \"Demo Manager\",\n  \"customerEmail\": \"demo@enterprise.com\",\n  \"subject\": \"Demo ticket — created during presentation\",\n  \"body\": \"This ticket was created live during the SupportIQ management demo to show the ticket creation flow.\",\n  \"source\": \"EMAIL\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/tickets",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "tickets"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new support ticket. The `ticketId` collection variable is automatically set for use in subsequent requests."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "02 List All Tickets",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Returns array', () => pm.expect(j).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('Has seeded tickets', () => pm.expect(j.length).to.be.gte(20));",
                  "console.log('Total tickets: ' + j.length);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/tickets",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "tickets"]
            },
            "description": "Fetch all tickets. Shows the raw unanalysed queue — use this in ACT 1 of the demo."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "03 List Open Tickets",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('All tickets are OPEN', () => j.forEach(t => pm.expect(t.status).to.eql('OPEN')));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/tickets?status=OPEN",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "tickets"],
              "query": [{ "key": "status", "value": "OPEN" }]
            },
            "description": "Filter tickets by status. Supported values: OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, ESCALATED, RESOLVED, CLOSED."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "04 Get Ticket by ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has id', () => pm.expect(j.id).to.be.a('number'));",
                  "pm.test('Has ticketNumber', () => pm.expect(j.ticketNumber).to.be.a('string'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/tickets/{{ticketId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Get a single ticket. Change `ticketId` variable (1-20) to view different demo tickets."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "05 Update Ticket Status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status updated', () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('IN_PROGRESS'));",
                  "pm.test('Agent assigned', () => pm.expect(j.assignedAgent).to.eql('Alex Rivera'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"IN_PROGRESS\",\n  \"assignedAgent\": \"Alex Rivera\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Update ticket status and optionally assign an agent. Valid statuses: OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, ESCALATED, RESOLVED, CLOSED."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "06 Delete Ticket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/tickets/{{ticketId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Delete a ticket. Use only on tickets you created — avoid deleting seeded demo tickets 1-20."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 — AI Intelligence (DEMO CORE)",
      "description": "The five AI-powered endpoints — the heart of the SupportIQ demo.\n\nRecommended demo order:\n  Dashboard → Raw Analyze → Draft Reply → Ticket Analyze → Bulk Triage → Escalation Queue",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 AI Dashboard  ★ ACT 2",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has queueHealthScore', () => pm.expect(j.queueHealthScore).to.be.within(0, 100));",
                  "pm.test('Has queueStatus', () => pm.expect(['HEALTHY','AT_RISK','CRITICAL']).to.include(j.queueStatus));",
                  "pm.test('Has aiRecommendations', () => pm.expect(j.aiRecommendations).to.be.an('array').with.length.gte(1));",
                  "console.log('Queue Health: ' + j.queueHealthScore + '/100 — ' + j.queueStatus);",
                  "console.log('Escalated: ' + j.escalatedCount + ' | Open: ' + j.openCount);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/dashboard",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "dashboard"]
            },
            "description": "ACT 2 — AI-powered queue health dashboard.\n\nComputes live queue statistics, then asks AI to score queue health (0-100), determine status (HEALTHY/AT_RISK/CRITICAL), identify top issues, and generate actionable recommendations.\n\nKey fields to highlight in the demo:\n- queueHealthScore + queueStatus\n- aiRecommendations (specific, not generic)\n- escalationAlert (null if none, urgent text if needed)\n- categoryBreakdown (shows dominant issue types)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "02 Analyze Raw Email  ★ ACT 3 (HERO)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has category', () => pm.expect(j.category).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('Has sentimentScore', () => pm.expect(j.sentimentScore).to.be.within(1, 10));",
                  "pm.test('Has riskScore', () => pm.expect(j.riskScore).to.be.within(1, 10));",
                  "pm.test('Has escalationRequired', () => pm.expect(j.escalationRequired).to.be.a('boolean'));",
                  "pm.test('Has keyIssues', () => pm.expect(j.keyIssues).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "console.log('Category: ' + j.category);",
                  "console.log('Sentiment: ' + j.sentimentScore + '/10 — ' + j.sentimentLabel);",
                  "console.log('Risk: ' + j.riskScore + '/10 | Escalate: ' + j.escalationRequired);",
                  "console.log('Priority: ' + j.suggestedPriority);",
                  "console.log('Key Issues: ' + JSON.stringify(j.keyIssues));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"rawText\": \"I am absolutely furious. Your system charged my corporate credit card TWICE for the annual plan — $2,400 was debited this morning on top of the charge last week. This is completely unacceptable and I am ready to dispute this with my bank and report this to the consumer protection agency. If this is not resolved TODAY I will be cancelling all 50 seats of our enterprise subscription and moving to a competitor.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/support/ai/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "support", "ai", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "ACT 3 — THE HERO ENDPOINT. Paste any raw customer email — no ticket needed.\n\nAI returns in ~2 seconds:\n- category (BILLING/TECHNICAL/ACCOUNT/COMPLAINT/REFUND/GENERAL)\n- sentimentScore 1-10 + sentimentLabel\n- riskScore 1-10 (churn / legal / escalation risk)\n- escalationRequired true/false\n- keyIssues (AI-extracted problems)\n- suggestedPriority (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL)\n- recommendedAction + estimatedResolutionTime\n- urgencyFactors (specific signals found)\n\nSwap the rawText for any customer email to show it works on anything."
          }
        },
